        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T00:39:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "at the same time - this is retroactively extending the HAL interfaces to add more. Shouldn\u0027t I also -2 this if it is already \"frozen\"? New APIs which are added here should be subjected to the same restrictions as new APIs which are added elsewhere. :D",
      "parentUuid": "b4517144_a3dc9058",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0bf56f4_1e7c3a8c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T00:50:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change addresses a defect revealed by a vendor, please see the bug. There is a \u0027no patch no waiver\u0027 policy, so we must provide a fix. It seems to me that the aforementioned policy conflicts with the policy of \u0027frozen interfaces.\u0027 Thankfully, we are not really modifying an interface, just a schema for the data. If you wish to oppose this change, please provide an alternative solution to this problem.",
      "parentUuid": "bb74f1cf_0aa50a92",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1bdd280_ed194f54",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
