        "id": 1153368
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-11T23:10:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will this lead to test regressions for folks who already launched their Audio Hal V6 devices?",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bec7722b_522f6675",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T00:12:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. This change, in its current form, only extends the list of values that vendors can use.",
      "parentUuid": "c1bdd280_ed194f54",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f05214d4_64c1452a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T00:13:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Robin brings in a good point. If we start requiring retroactively that vendor extension values must follow a certain format (e.g. being namespaced) this can, and will lead to regressions in VTS that were previously passing.",
      "parentUuid": "a0bf56f4_1e7c3a8c",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca4b0dab_44e820ec",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T19:26:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does that mean there was another change that added this restriction after the original release of 6.0? Or was the 6.0 interface released in this form?",
      "parentUuid": "f05214d4_64c1452a",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "960092e8_77faca69",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T20:51:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The latter. There are two types for audio formats: the set of enum values, and the one that allows vendor extensions on top of them. We should be using the second type consistently through the schema, however there were a couple of places where we forgot to do that.\n\nThanks for approving!",
      "parentUuid": "ca4b0dab_44e820ec",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c88f689_24e295b8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T20:53:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Eric, could you please give a +2.\n\nRobin, could you please give a Dr. No\u0027s approval.",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "495e9539_d85c4f56",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T21:31:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the 5.0/6.0 interface was released in this form (even if 4.0 allowed it), then this constitutes an addition of new APIs. Certainly, it may be the case that devices before that used extensions, but CMIIR _no_ extensions were allowed in 5.0/6.0 (hence this bug + backport). The vendor is requesting an addition of new APIs here, to satisfy a usecase that was accidentally no longer supported (this is a huge inconvenience, but they could always create a custom interface). So - I don\u0027t exactly see how/why we can dismiss namespaces here out of hand. Can we see if these vendors would accept namespaces? At the least, can we recommend namespaces here? Is there something I\u0027m missing?",
      "parentUuid": "960092e8_77faca69",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7ed8a91_58ae9ceb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T21:32:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We should be using the second type consistently through the schema, however there were a couple of places where we forgot to do that.\n\nWe should also be namespacing vendor extensions consistently. Is there any place this is missing in 7.0?",
      "parentUuid": "495e9539_d85c4f56",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18be2756_ed75557b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T22:33:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e but CMIIR _no_ extensions were allowed in 5.0/6.0 (hence this bug + backport).\n\nThis isn\u0027t correct. Use of vendor-extended types for audio devices and formats (in XSD, at least) was allowed even in 4.0: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/audio/4.0/config/audio_policy_configuration.xsd;l\u003d366;drc\u003dd3f6a411500f6b5deaa575773b5111dd58100914\n\nIn 5.0 we have added a couple more fields of audio format type into XSD. And we have made a mistake of using the enum-only type (\u0027audioFormat\u0027) instead of the type that allows enums and vendor extensions (\u0027extendableAudioFormat\u0027) for these new fields.\n\nThat means, vendors could already have vendor extensions for audio formats in their audio policy manager configuration files, however they could not use them consistently for all the fields that carry an audio format value. This is the bug we are fixing.\n\nCould you please explain why are you considering this as a request to add a new API?\n\n\u003e We should also be namespacing vendor extensions consistently. Is there any place this is missing in 7.0?\n\nI haven\u0027t fixed the bug that asks to namespace vendor extensions. I will do that soon.",
      "parentUuid": "b7ed8a91_58ae9ceb",
      "revId": "b4d10f0109fbf7e33c9f3e3e1391a4383c9686d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
  ]
